actions.message:
Topic: {{topic}}

FIRST write the deliverable. Call md_file with action=write, path=docs/sop/avenger-<slug>.md. The file MUST open with a one-page SUMMARY of at most 60 lines, readable by someone who will never open the detail, in this order: (1) three to five plain sentences - what this field is and how the money moves in it, one idea per sentence; (2) the foothold as four sentences, each followed by the single fact that supports it - who pays / what they buy instead today / why the incumbent leaves that work alone / what it costs one person to hold it; (3) the landscape in one or two sentences - which segments are already levelled and which one is still open (the table belongs to the detail); (4) build vs reuse - one conclusion sentence plus three bullets; (5) the thinnest pillar - one short paragraph naming what this map rests on with the least evidence; (6) the five unproven facts, one line each with what would settle it; (7) your plain judgment - 8-12 sentences, first person, no hedging, ending with one action testable this week. If the file exceeds 8KB, continue with action=append chunks until every section is on disk, then read the tail back with read_file(start_line=...) to prove the summary survived. Then call write_avenger_doc with the same Markdown.

Your narration from the last round:
{{judgment.prev}}

Write the FINAL consolidated report as ONE Markdown document, merging the line reports (read docs/sop/avenger_<slug>_*.md with file_requests if you need the details back). Below the summary: one section per line with exactly four blocks - 查了什么 / 查到什么 (3-5 facts, EACH ending with its line id marker such as [MKT-03], value + source + date) / 怎么推的 (the logic chain, 3-5 steps) / 什么条件下会错. Then the evidence table - the 来源 cell of every row ends with the id marker - the local unknowns, and the gaps of this map. THE BODY MUST CARRY THE MARKERS INLINE: a list of ids only in the closing section is NOT a citation layer and the merge has failed if the tables have none. Every sentence in the summary that states a number or a named fact ends with its id marker; a claim you cannot mark is deleted, not softened. Follow the writing rules in your system prompt: one bullet one fact, no grades in the prose, gloss every term of the field on first use, no table inside the summary. Every fact carries its line id marker ([MKT-01], [USR-01], ...) and the document ends with a 参考文献 section, one entry per id: [MKT-07] Title -- URL -- opened DATE, or '... -- search snippet only'. Do not renumber the ids. There is no go/no-go verdict and no action plan in this document. Do not reply only DONE.
